{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:12:15Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 78, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Write", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01U1BiDVWBuGtZtEJs3qvJUk", "input": {"file_path": "/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/design.md", "content": "# Design: Show how many tasks are left\n\nTaiga #10 \u00b7 reads `docs/spec.md`\n\n## Summary\n\nOne new read-only status line, `TaskCounts`, placed directly under the\n`<h1>Tasks</h1>` title and above `AddTask`. It shows the true open/done\ntotals (never the filtered subset), pluralizes correctly, and is hidden\nduring the initial load \u2014 matching acceptance criteria 1\u20133 and 8. No new UI\nlibrary, icon, or token system: it reuses the page's existing type scale and\nadds one new (computed, AA-passing) muted-grey shade in the same family as\nthe existing `#6b7780` used for `.loading`/`.empty`.\n\n## Placement decision\n\nTwo candidates per spec: inside `.list-toolbar` (next to `TaskFilter` /\n`ClearCompleted`), or near the `<h1>`. Going with **near the `<h1>`**:\n\n- `.list-toolbar` today holds exactly two flex children with\n  `justify-content: space-between` (`frontend/src/App.css:33-40`). A third\n  child changes that layout's balance and its wrap behavior at narrow\n  widths \u2014 avoidable by not touching it.\n- The count is not a filter or an action, it's a summary fact about the\n  whole list (spec: \"not the filtered/visible subset\"). Placing it away from\n  `TaskFilter` reduces the chance a user reads it as filter-scoped.\n- A summary line directly under the title is the conventional placement for\n  \"N items left\" in task-tracker UIs, and reads first, before any controls.\n\n## Component\n\nNew file: `frontend/src/components/TaskCounts.jsx`, sibling to\n`ClearCompleted.jsx` (same one-prop-object, no-internal-state shape):\n\n```jsx\nexport default function TaskCounts({ open, done }) {\n  return (\n    <p className=\"task-counts\" role=\"status\">\n      {open} {open === 1 ? 'task' : 'tasks'} open \u00b7 {done} {done === 1 ? 'task' : 'tasks'} done\n    </p>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n- `role=\"status\"` gives an implicit `aria-live=\"polite\"` + `aria-atomic=\"true\"`\n  region: when add/complete/delete/clear-completed change the numbers,\n  assistive tech announces the new sentence without moving focus away from\n  whatever control the user just used. No other element in this app has a\n  live region today, but this is exactly the case ARIA's `status` role\n  exists for \u2014 a passive text update caused by an action elsewhere on the\n  page.\n- Separator is a middle dot (`\u00b7`, U+00B7) \u2014 visually splits the two clauses\n  without implying a list or a sentence boundary. Screen readers render it\n  as a brief pause; the sentence stays parseable either way.\n- No `count` prop naming collision with `ClearCompleted`'s `count` \u2014 this\n  takes `open`/`done` since it carries two numbers, named after the same\n  vocabulary as `TaskFilter`'s `open`/`done` filter values\n  (`frontend/src/components/TaskFilter.jsx:1-5`) for consistency.\n\n## Wiring in `App.jsx`\n\n`frontend/src/App.jsx:38` already computes `completedCount`. Add the open\ncount the same way (filter over `tasks`, never `visibleTasks`/`sortedTasks`,\nper acceptance criterion 1):\n\n```jsx\nconst completedCount = tasks.filter((t) => t.done).length\nconst openCount = tasks.filter((t) => !t.done).length\n```\n\nRender, gated on `!loading` (criterion 8 \u2014 no count during initial load):\n\n```jsx\n<h1>Tasks</h1>\n{!loading && <TaskCounts open={openCount} done={completedCount} />}\n<AddTask onAdd={(title, priority) => run(() => api.createTask(title, priority))} />\n```\n\nImport alongside the other component imports:\n`import TaskCounts from './components/TaskCounts'`.\n\nNothing else in `App.jsx` changes. `visibleTasks`/`sortedTasks`/`filter`\nstay untouched \u2014 `TaskCounts` only ever reads `tasks`.\n\n## CSS \u2014 `frontend/src/App.css`\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. Tighten `h1`'s bottom margin so the new line sits snug under the title,\n   with the original visual gap now living between the counts line and\n   `AddTask`:\n\n   ```diff\n   - h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }\n   + h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }\n   ```\n\n2. Add the new rule (place near `.empty, .loading` since it's the same kind\n   of secondary status text):\n\n   ```css\n   .task-counts {\n     margin: 0 0 1.2rem;\n     font-size: 0.95rem;\n     color: #5a646c;\n   }\n   ```\n\n### Contrast check (new colour pairing)\n\n`.task-counts` sits directly on the page background (`body { background:\n#f6f7f8 }` \u2014 it's not inside a white `.task` card), so that's the pairing to\ncheck, same as `.loading`/`.empty` already on that background today.\n\nThe obvious reuse, the existing muted grey `#6b7780`, **fails**: computed\nrelative luminance 0.1788 (text) vs. 0.9289 (`#f6f7f8`) \u2192 contrast\n**4.28:1**, below the 4.5:1 text minimum. (`.loading`/`.empty` already use\nthis pairing \u2014 pre-existing, out of scope to fix here per the story's\nnon-goals, but not a pairing to copy forward into new UI.)\n\nDarkened to `#5a646c`, same hue/family, adjusted lightness only: computed\nluminance 0.1238 vs. 0.9289 \u2192 contrast **5.63:1** \u2014 passes 4.5:1 with\nmargin. This keeps the \"secondary, muted\" meaning intact rather than\nswitching to a token (e.g. full-strength `#16191c` body text) that would\nread as equally prominent as task titles.\n\n## States\n\n**Loading** (`loading === true`, before first fetch resolves):\n```\nTasks\n[Add task...]                    [Add]\n```\nNo counts line at all \u2014 `{!loading && <TaskCounts .../>}` renders nothing.\nMatches the existing gate at `App.jsx:60-71` (criterion 8).\n\n**Populated \u2014 typical (mixed open/done):**\n```\nTasks\n3 tasks open \u00b7 2 tasks done\n[Add task...]                    [Add]\n```\n\n**Populated \u2014 zero tasks (criterion 2):**\n```\nTasks\n0 tasks open \u00b7 0 tasks done\n[Add task...]                    [Add]\n```\nBoth numbers still render \u2014 never blank, never hidden, plural grammar for\n`0` in both buckets.\n\n**Populated \u2014 exactly one task, singular grammar (criterion 3):**\n```\nTasks\n1 task open \u00b7 0 tasks done\n```\nand independently, after completing it:\n```\nTasks\n0 tasks open \u00b7 1 task done\n```\nEach clause pluralizes independently \u2014 `open === 1` and `done === 1` are\nchecked separately, so one bucket can be singular while the other is\nplural.\n\n**Populated \u2014 one bucket empty, other many (edge case: \"all open\" / \"all\ndone\"):**\n```\nTasks\n5 tasks open \u00b7 0 tasks done\n```\n`0` still reads as plural (\"0 tasks\"), never suppressed.\n\n**Error** (`error` set, criterion 9): `tasks` retains its last-known value\n(`refresh()` doesn't clear it on failure), so `TaskCounts` keeps rendering\nthe last-known-good numbers, unchanged, below the existing error banner:\n```\nTasks\n2 tasks open \u00b7 1 task done\nCould not reach the server            <- existing .error banner, unchanged\n[Add task...]                    [Add]\n```\n\n**Interactive:** none. `TaskCounts` renders static text with no button,\nlink, or focusable element \u2014 there is nothing to focus, hover, or disable.\nIts only \"interactivity\" is the `aria-live` announcement described above,\nwhich is passive (triggered by actions on other controls, not on itself).\n\n## Traceability\n\n| Acceptance criterion | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Open + done counts visible, from full `tasks` not filtered subset | `TaskCounts` fed `openCount`/`completedCount`, both derived from `tasks` in `App.jsx`, never `visibleTasks`/`sortedTasks` |\n| 2. Zero tasks \u2192 shows `0`, not blank/hidden | \"Populated \u2014 zero tasks\" state above; component always renders both numbers, no conditional suppression |\n| 3. Singular/plural grammar at exactly 1, independent per bucket | `{open === 1 ? 'task' : 'tasks'}` / `{done === 1 ? 'task' : 'tasks'}` \u2014 independent ternaries in `TaskCounts.jsx` |\n| 4\u20137. Stays correct across add/complete/delete/clear-completed, no reload | No local state in `TaskCounts` \u2014 pure props from `tasks`, recomputed every render via the existing `run()` \u2192 `refresh()` cycle (`App.jsx:40-49`), same mechanism `completedCount` already relies on |\n| 8. Hidden while loading | `{!loading && <TaskCounts .../>}` in `App.jsx` |\n| 9. Error state doesn't break/blank the count | No design change needed \u2014 `tasks` isn't cleared on error, so `TaskCounts` naturally keeps its last values; verified in \"Error\" state above |\n\n## Non-goals honored\n\nNo per-priority breakdown, no persistence, no change to `TaskFilter` or\n`ClearCompleted` behavior, no backend/API touch \u2014 matches `docs/spec.md`'s\nNon-goals section. `frontend/src/api.js` is untouched.\n\n## Files touched\n\n- New: `frontend/src/components/TaskCounts.jsx`\n- Edit: `frontend/src/App.jsx` (import, two derived variables, one render\n  line)\n- Edit: `frontend/src/App.css` (one rule added, one existing rule's\n  bottom-margin adjusted)\n"}, "session_id": "335dcd2f-bfda-4ed8-a78c-7465095ee02c"}}
