{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:12:21Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 80, "kind": "message", "text": "Wrote `docs/design.md`. Summary for the next stage:\n\n- **New component:** `frontend/src/components/TaskCounts.jsx` \u2014 takes `open`/`done` props, renders `\"{n} task(s) open \u00b7 {n} task(s) done\"` with independent singular/plural per bucket, `role=\"status\"` for live-region announcements.\n- **Placement:** directly under `<h1>Tasks</h1>`, gated on `!loading`, rather than inside `.list-toolbar` (kept that layout untouched).\n- **Wiring:** add `openCount = tasks.filter((t) => !t.done).length` next to the existing `completedCount` in `App.jsx:38`.\n- **CSS:** new `.task-counts` rule using `#5a646c` (a darkened, contrast-verified version of the existing muted grey \u2014 the obvious reuse, `#6b7780`, actually fails AA at 4.28:1 on the page background, so I computed a passing alternative at 5.63:1) plus a small `h1` margin tweak.\n- All 9 acceptance criteria traced to specific design elements, including loading/error/zero/singular edge cases with ASCII wireframes.\n\nNext stage (developer) should read `docs/design.md` for exact code and CSS to implement.", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "335dcd2f-bfda-4ed8-a78c-7465095ee02c"}}
